# D-134 — THE MANIFEST-SHAPE VALIDATOR'S MEMBERSHIP, DERIVED OVER THE PACKAGE.
#
# THIS IS A RED RULE AS SHIPPED, AND THAT IS THE DELIVERABLE. The six readers
# named in the VERDICT block below are live instances of the escalated class;
# the rule exists to make them visible and to stay red until they close.
# `test_every_manifest_record_reader_in_the_package_establishes_the_shape` is
# the assertion, and it is the single failing test in the suite at this commit.
#
# THE HARM, driven live against the real _DISPATCH with
# castings/manifest.json = {"castings": "nope"} and {"castings": [1,2,3]}:
#
#   Foundry-Validate-Castings  AttributeError: 'str' object has no attribute 'get'
#   Foundry-Next               the identical AttributeError, via
#                              _compute_next_action -> _check_streams_complete
#                              -> _check_sight_required
#   Foundry-Gate               AttributeError: 'int'/'str' object has no attribute 'get'
#   _trace_skip_check          AttributeError: 'int'/'str' object has no attribute 'get'
#   _append_to_manifest_evidence_provenance
#                              AttributeError: 'int' object has no attribute 'get'
#
# Foundry-Next is the mandatory handshake before EVERY phase transition, so
# this is the most-travelled door in the tool surface, not an edge case.
#
# THE DEFECT NAMED TWO. THE SCAN FOUND SIX, and the four it added were all
# driven and all raise. That is the argument for the scan: D-132's fix routed
# foundry_spawn.py's four readers through one declaration and left every other
# module's reader indexing records unguarded, which is the escalated class
# recurring one door over — a hardening bound to the site that reported it.
#
# WHY THE PROPERTY IS NOT "IS THE KEY DECLARED". At D-132 both spawn doors DID
# call the guard — at the top rung, and then indexed the records below it.
# `_check_sight_required` indexes castings[].key_files, which _MANIFEST_SHAPE
# declares perfectly well, and still raises, because it never asks the
# validator anything. Presence of a declaration was never the property.
# COVERAGE of the rung a reader indexes is.
#
# ALL THREE AXES ARE DERIVED, which is what the cycle-19 ruling requires of a
# fix whose derivation itself has axes:
#
#   which files    rglob over BOTH shipped source trees, located from the
#                  package's own __file__ and cross-checked against an
#                  independent os.walk, so a root that moves fails loudly
#                  instead of scanning nothing.
#   which rungs    walked out of _MANIFEST_SHAPE. castings[].key_files and
#                  waves[].casting_ids are lists of NON-records (element shape
#                  None — the table's explicit statement that the reader below
#                  is on its own), so they are correctly not rungs, and
#                  stream_skips is excluded by that same rule rather than by an
#                  exception written for it.
#   which readers  taint from the "manifest.json" literal, propagated ACROSS
#                  CALLS (foundry_validate.py#_fingerprint_inputs indexes a
#                  document it never loaded) and through path-building helpers
#                  (evidence.py#_resolve_manifest_path owns the literal and its
#                  callers never see one). A scan following only the literal
#                  reports both of those modules clean.
#
# THE ALLOW-LIST IS EMPTY. scripts/validate_intent_coverage.py's
# load_manifest_casting_ids reads the same document and is not an offender
# because it isinstance-guards the rung it indexes — recognised BY THE RULE,
# and the function is not named anywhere in the test module. foundry_spawn.py
# is clean because it routes through the validator, so the provider of the
# shared validator is a member of its own rule rather than its exception.
#

